export const RAW_CHANGELOG_MD = "# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to **Crease (`crease-api`)** are documented in this file.\n\nThis repository is the **single source of truth** for release notes, powering both `/changelog` and `GET /api/v1/changelog`.  \nThe format adheres to [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), [Semantic Versioning 2.0.0](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html), and [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).\n\n---\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n_No unreleased changes yet. Add new entries under `feat`, `fix`, `security`, `perf`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, or `build` before running `npm run release -- <version>`._\n\n---\n\n## [0.0.0] - 2026-04-12 — Genesis: Cloudflare-Native Cricket Edge Architecture\n\nInitial architectural rebuild from scratch establishing **Crease (`crease-api` / `crease-edge`)** as a dedicated, Cricket-Only, Cloudflare Workers (`workerd`)-native Edge API. Preserves 100% of the reverse-engineered CS3 cryptographic pipelines in pure Web Standards (`Uint8Array` + `crypto.subtle`) while introducing a collision-free cricket ontology, tiered edge caching, hardened streaming, and interactive developer tooling.\n\n### Features\n\n- `feat(edge):` **Cloudflare Workers (`workerd`) Native Runtime Foundation** — Built a zero-Node, zero-`Buffer`, zero-`Bun.*` Worker entry exporting both HTTP `fetch` and 2-minute Cron `scheduled` handlers (`wrangler.jsonc`), backed by typed `CreaseEnv` bindings (`CREASE_KV`, Cache API `caches.default`, isolate-safe L1 LRU, and graceful zero-binding fallback).\n- `feat(crypto):` **Pure-Edge Cryptographic Engine Across All 6 CS3 Providers** — Re-implemented all native Dalvik (`classes.dex`) decryption pipelines exclusively using Web Crypto (`crypto.subtle`) and `Uint8Array`: Cricify 4-tier AES-128-CBC + `EnvelopeCrypto`, Sportzx pure-TS SXR3 ChaCha20-variant sponge + 128-bit MAC (Dex & Legacy layouts) + AES fallbacks, PlayFy Dalvik 32-bit FNV-1a (`0x811c9dc5`) key/IV derivation + PKCS#7/NoPadding AES-128-CBC, SKTech 64-hex header stripping + Lookup Table D + V23 byte-pair swap/reverse, PlayZTV `libplayztv.so` reverse/pair-swap/substitution, and LivXow multi-pass substitution + Base64url `pro/*.txt` decoding.\n- `feat(providers):` **Resilient 6-Provider CS3 Federation & Singleflight Remote Config** — Implemented unified adapters for `cricify`, `sportzx`, `playfy`, `sktech`, `playztv`, and `livxow` with singleflight Firebase Remote Config fetching (6-hour L1/KV cache), zero self-sabotage mirror domain failover, multi-format date/time parsing (`DD/MM/YYYY`, `HH:mm:ss`, Unix epochs), `#KODIPROP` ClearKey M3U8 parsing, and per-provider circuit breakers.\n- `feat(domain):` **Cricket-First Domain Ontology & Collision-Free Squad Graph** — Authored a dedicated cricket taxonomy covering 9 formats (`TEST`, `ODI`, `T20I`, `T20`, `T10`, `HUNDRED`, `LIST_A`, `FIRST_CLASS`, `OTHER`), 9 squad classes (`MENS`, `WOMENS`, `U19_MENS`, `U19_WOMENS`, `A_TEAM`, `LEGENDS`, `FRANCHISE`, `DOMESTIC`, `CLUB`), collision-free canonical squad resolution (`IND` vs `IND-W` vs `IND-U19` vs `IND-A`; `MI` vs `MI-W` vs `MICT` vs `MINY` vs `MIE`), strict non-cricket filtering, order-independent canonical fixture deduplication, and deterministic stream quality/commentary ranking.\n- `feat(search):` **Weighted Damerau-Levenshtein Cricket Search Engine** — Added categorized search across matches, series, squads, and 24/7 channels with 1-edit typo & adjacent-character transposition tolerance (e.g., `\"Indai\"` → `IND` / India matches) plus live-match priority boosting.\n- `feat(streaming):` **24KB Manifest Inspector & 6-Scheme Edge Stream Proxy** — Added bounded 24KB HLS/DASH manifest inspection (renditions, codecs, audio languages, LL-HLS/LL-DASH flags, ClearKey/AES-128/SAMPLE-AES/CENC detection, and player compatibility matrix) alongside a 6-scheme (`cricify://`, `sportzx://`, `playfy://`, `sktech://`, `playztv://`, `livxow://`) and HTTPS edge proxy supporting HLS/DASH quality filtering and signed CDN query token inheritance.\n- `feat(api):` **Versioned `/api/v1` Surface, XMLTV EPG, IPTV M3U8 & Edge SSE** — Delivered 28 typed routes under `/api/v1` using a uniform `{ ok, data, meta, error }` envelope, `ETag`/`304 Not Modified` conditional responses, dynamic XMLTV EPG (`/api/v1/epg.xml`), IPTV M3U8 playlists (`/api/v1/playlist.m3u`), bounded `TransformStream` live SSE (`/api/v1/live/sse`), and OpenAPI 3.1.0 specification (`/openapi.json`).\n- `feat(ui):` **Cricket Workbench Portal, Interactive OpenAPI Docs & Live Changelog** — Built the Crease Cricket Match Explorer & 24KB Manifest Inspector (`/portal`), Interactive OpenAPI 3.1.0 Request Runner (`/docs`), and dynamic `CHANGELOG.md`-backed Release Ledger (`/changelog` + `/api/v1/changelog` + `/changelog.md`).\n\n### Security\n\n- `security(ssrf):` **Airtight SSRF Guard with Alternate IP & Redirect Hop Validation** — Blocked loopback, RFC1918 private ranges, CGNAT (`100.64.0.0/10`), link-local/cloud metadata (`169.254.169.254`), IPv6 ULA/link-local/IPv4-mapped literals, decimal/hex/octal/shorthand IP bypasses, embedded URL userinfo, non-HTTP(S) schemes, and unvalidated `3xx` redirect targets across both manifest probing and edge proxying with zero localhost exemptions.\n- `security(headers):` **Strict Credential Redaction & Proxy Header Allowlisting** — Stripped `Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Set-Cookie`, and `X-Api-Key` headers from all public API responses (`hasRedactedAuth` metadata flag) and restricted forwarded proxy headers to a strict allowlist with CRLF injection filtering.\n- `security(validation):` **Zod Schema Validation & Safe DOM Rendering** — Validated all query parameters via strict Zod schemas and constructed all browser UI views using safe DOM APIs (`createElement`/`textContent`) without raw HTML string interpolation of untrusted data.\n\n### Performance\n\n- `perf(cache):` **Subrequest-Budgeted 3-Tier Edge Caching with Cron SWR** — Decoupled heavy CS3 provider fan-out onto the 2-minute Cloudflare Cron Trigger writing precomputed snapshots to KV; live HTTP requests serve in sub-millisecond time from L1 Isolate LRU → Cloudflare Cache API (`caches.default`) → KV with non-blocking `ctx.waitUntil()` stale-while-revalidate refreshes.\n- `perf(prober):` **24KB Bounded Stream Reads & Singleflight Coalescing** — Capped upstream manifest inspection reads at 24KB via `ReadableStream` early cancellation to prevent Worker memory/CPU spikes, and coalesced concurrent Firebase Remote Config and catalog refresh calls per isolate.\n- `perf(sse):` **Bounded 55-Second Edge SSE Lifecycle** — Implemented `TransformStream`-based Server-Sent Events with periodic heartbeats and clean client-reconnect termination within Cloudflare Workers wall-clock limits.\n\n### Testing & Verification\n\n- `test(crypto):` **Deterministic Golden Vector Suite for All 6 CS3 Ciphers** — Locked down exact key/IV derivations, SXR3 sponge MAC verification, PlayFy Dalvik FNV-1a (`\"BR4weRP=5A/Y&8%5\"` / `\"Va+XYCKnkinUMDvk\"`), SKTech Lookup Table D / V23, PlayZTV byte-swap, LivXow substitution, and `EnvelopeCrypto` round-trips.\n- `test(domain):` **Cricket Ontology, Classifier, Deduplication & Changelog Parser Tests** — Verified zero non-cricket leakage, Men's/Women's/U19/A-Team/MI franchise collision prevention, order-independent canonical match IDs, typo-tolerant search, and structured `CHANGELOG.md` parsing.\n- `test(streaming):` **SSRF Bypass Matrix, Redirect Re-Validation & Manifest Parser Tests** — Verified blocking of private/metadata/alternate-encoded IPs, redirect hops to internal hosts, HLS/DASH ClearKey/AES-128 parsing, and DASH quality filtering.\n- `test(api):` **End-to-End Cloudflare Worker HTTP Contract Suite** — Verified `/health`, `/openapi.json`, `/api/v1/matches`, `ETag`/`304`, `/api/v1/changelog`, `/changelog.md`, SSRF 403 enforcement, and zero legacy brand leakage.\n\n### Documentation & Tooling\n\n- `docs(blueprint):` **Principal Engineering Architecture Blueprint (`plan.md`)** — Documented the complete forensic audit delta, subrequest budget, cricket domain ontology, edge storage topology, security posture, and SemVer roadmap.\n- `build(release):` **Zero-Drift Changelog Sync & SemVer Release Automation** — Added `scripts/sync-changelog.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, and static edge-compatibility lint gates (`scripts/lint.ts`) verifying version lockstep across `package.json`, `src/config/env.ts`, and `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Release Governance & Commit Legend\n\n| Prefix | Category | SemVer Bump | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `feat(scope):` | Features | `MINOR` (`0.x.0`) | New endpoints, cricket ontology capabilities, provider adapters, or UI workflows |\n| `fix(scope):` | Bug Fixes | `PATCH` (`0.0.x`) | Defect corrections, parser edge cases, upstream decryption compatibility fixes |\n| `security(scope):` | Security | `PATCH` (`0.0.x`) | SSRF rules, header redaction, input validation, and dependency hardening |\n| `perf(scope):` | Performance | `PATCH` (`0.0.x`) | Cache tiering, subrequest reductions, bundle size or latency optimizations |\n| `refactor(scope):` | Refactoring | `PATCH` (`0.0.x`) | Internal structural improvements without external contract changes |\n| `test(scope):` | Testing | — | Golden vectors, unit tests, contract tests, and browser verification coverage |\n| `docs(scope):` | Documentation | — | `README.md`, `plan.md`, OpenAPI 3.1 schema, and changelog updates |\n| `build(scope):` | Build & Tooling | — | Wrangler config, TypeScript config, lint gates, and release scripts |\n| `type(scope)!:` | Breaking Change | `MAJOR` (`x.0.0`) | Backwards-incompatible `/api/v1` contract or binding changes |\n\n[Unreleased]: https://github.com/crease-api/crease/compare/v0.0.0...HEAD\n[0.0.0]: https://github.com/crease-api/crease/releases/tag/v0.0.0\n";
